Vikram and Betal: The Clever Farmer

King Vikram was once again carrying Betal through the forest.

Betal began another story.

“Once, there was a poor farmer,” said Betal. “He worked very hard but had very little money.”

One day, he found a bag of gold coins in his field.

The farmer thought, “This must belong to someone. I should not keep it.”

Soon, a merchant came looking for his lost gold.

The farmer returned the bag to him.

The merchant checked it and said, “Some coins are missing! You must have taken them!”

The farmer was shocked.

The case was taken to the king.

The king listened carefully and then said, “If the bag truly belonged to the merchant, he would know the exact number of coins.”

The merchant stayed silent.

The king realized the truth and punished the greedy merchant.

The honest farmer was rewarded.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, who was right?”

Vikram replied, “The king was right because he trusted honesty.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Honesty always wins over greed.
